-- title:
--   Counting ⟨ S⟩-orbits on SL₂(ℤ)/Γ₀(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a natural number, assumed non-zero. Consider the coset space $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\Gamma_0(N)$, where $\Gamma_0(N)$ is the congruence subgroup of matrices in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ that are upper triangular modulo $N$, and let the cyclic subgroup $\langle S\rangle$ generated by $S=\begin{pmatrix}0&-1\\1&0\end{pmatrix}$ act on this coset space by left translation. The assertion is an equality of natural numbers: twice the number of orbits of this action, that is twice the cardinality of the quotient of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\Gamma_0(N)$ by the orbit equivalence relation of $\langle S\rangle$, equals $\psi(N)+\nu_2(N)$. Here $\psi(N)$ is defined as the sum of $N/d$ over the squarefree divisors $d$ of $N$ (so $\psi(N)=N\prod_{p\mid N}(1+p^{-1})$), and $\nu_2(N)$ is defined as the number of elements $x$ of $\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z}$ with $x^2+1=0$. Since $S$ has order $4$ in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and $-I$ acts trivially on the coset space, every orbit has one or two elements, and the identity is equivalent to saying that the number of cosets fixed by $S$ is $\nu_2(N)$.
--
--   This is the classical count of the elliptic points of order $2$ on the modular curve $X_0(N)$, in the form $2\varepsilon_2=\psi(N)+\nu_2(N)$ with $\psi(N)=[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}):\Gamma_0(N)]$; the orbit count is the number of points of $X_0(N)$ above the elliptic point of order $2$ of $X(1)$. It feeds into the genus formula for $X_0(N)$, being used by [`ModularCurve.finrank_parabolicHoms_gamma0_le_two_mul_genusFormula`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_parabolicHoms_gamma0_le_two_mul_genusFormula).
